#  hostname_driver.icn -- the grading vehicle for procs/hostname.icn: hostname() reads the box's name through a pipe to
#  /usr/bin/hostname and keeps it in a static.  The name is the run's environment, so hostname_driver.pin pins it (the shim
#  answers "scriphost" to every process of the run, the piped command included) for the oracle and both SCRIP modes alike,
#  and the name is graded exactly (Lon CEO-1474, 2026-10-04).
link hostname
procedure main()
   write("hostname: ", hostname());
   write("again, from the static: ", hostname());
   write("length: ", *hostname());
end
